# Euroleague Fantasy

Personal Streamlit dashboard in this repo. Not a public site. Do not add accounts, hosting, or a new estimated-price model. Player and coach credits come from the official Fantasy Challenge list when Fan ID credentials are configured (`src/prices.py` / `src/official.py`), cached at `data/cache/fantasy_prices.parquet`. Otherwise players fall back to the public list and coach credits stay typed.

## Run

```bash
cd ~/euroleague-fantasy
python3 -m pip install -r requirements.txt
streamlit run app.py --server.port 8501
```

Open http://localhost:8501. On the same Wi‑Fi you can also use the Network URL (192.168.x). Do not run with `--server.headless true`; that prints a public External URL. Sidebar **Refresh data** updates box scores, prices, and the injury report. The first download is slow; later runs skip cached games. Cache lives in `data/cache/`. Squad file is `data/squad.json`. Do not re-download the full box-score cache unless the user asks to refresh.

`main()` in `app.py` runs at import so Streamlit AppTest executes the app. Leave that call in place.

## Scoring

Player fantasy is PIR on a loss and PIR × 1.10 on a win. Coach points follow the official margin buckets. A legal squad is 4 guards, 4 forwards, 2 centers, 100 credits, at most 6 players from one club, and at most 6 players on T1 (the first tip day of the round) when T2 or T3 still have games, so later-day players can replace a low T1 score. Best team spends leftover credits on a same-position upgrade when it does not lose projected points or break those rules. Starters, sixth man, and coach count in full. Bench counts at half. One starter is captain at 2×. Legal starting shapes (G-F-C): 2-2-1, 1-2-2, 2-1-2, 1-3-1, 3-1-1.

GP, Min, Fpts/g, Last 5, Exp min, floor, ceiling, and projected form use this season after one game, and last season only when there are zero games. Opponent matchup is the **game pie**: total fantasy G, F, or C scored vs that defense in a game, versus the league pie. One star center is that night's whole C pie, not cloned onto every opposing center. Forwards stay on the F pie. L3/L5/L10/ALL average those game pies this season. Factor is ALL versus the league, pulled toward last season until a few games are in. Then home/away, and a 10% win bonus weighted by win probability. When a teammate is Out or unconfirmed and still has as many current-season games as the rest of the club, remaining Available players get extra Exp min: 60% to the same position (G/F/C), 40% to the rest, in proportion to current expected minutes, capped at 38. If he already missed games in the sample, teammate averages already include that time and it is not added again. When he is Available again with fewer games than the club, that extra is taken back (same 60/40, scaled by the share of games he missed). Projected, floor, and ceiling scale with the minute change. Historical Min and Last 5 do not. Best team uses those projections.

## Columns

Green is the league’s top third, yellow the middle, red the bottom. Volatility is reversed. Price is not colored.

- **Status** Available when the player is confirmed to play. Yellow (Expected, Questionable, Game-time, Doubtful, Uncertain) means it is not confirmed. Out means he will not play. Players missing from the BasketNews injury report are Available. **Note** is the injury comment. Best team uses only Available players. **Pos** is G/F/C from the Fantasy Challenge list (official or givemestats), not the EuroLeague box-score Center/Forward label.
- **GP** games in the sample. **Min** average minutes. **Fpts/g** fantasy points per game. **Last 5** last five games. **Per 36** per 36 minutes. **Volatility** score swing.
- **Price** published credits. **Owned %** share of Fantasy Challenge managers who own him (official Fan ID list only; blank on the public list). **Points per credit** Fpts/g / Price (average of every game in the sample).
- **Projected** next-game expectation: Fpts/g times the opponent's G/F/C game pie versus the league (shrunk toward last season while the sample is small), then home/away and the win bonus, including extra minutes when a teammate is Out or unconfirmed. **Floor** / **Ceiling** low and high outcomes, scaled the same way. **Counted** Projected times captain 2×, starter or sixth 1×, or bench 0.5×.
- **Opp factor** / **Factor** the position's game-total fantasy vs the league, pulled toward last season until a few games are in. **L3 / L5 / L10 / ALL** average those pies. Forwards stay on F; they are not recoded as C.
- **Win %** / **Win chance** chance the club wins. **H/A** home or away. **Form** 2025-26, 2026-27, or Pos. avg. After one game this season, Form is this season; no last-year mix. Players without a game yet keep last season. Best team uses those projections, including the next-game matchup.
- **Slot** Captain, Starter, Sixth, or Bench. **Formation (G-F-C)** starters by position. Coach credits come from the official list when configured (shown on My team; editable overrides on Best team). **Credits** on Best team and My team budget checks use the Fantasy Challenge bank when known (players + coach), not a fixed 100. **Changes** prefills from official free trades left when Fan ID data is loaded (still compares Coming in/Going out to the local saved team). **Include coach in changes** lets Best team pick among priced coaches; unchecked keeps the saved team's coach. **Changes** 1–4 means replace that many from the saved team and keep the rest. All rebuilds. **Trade one player** (Best team expander) lists same-position upgrades at or below the dropped player's price; ranked by +Counted for his My team slot (min +1.0 projected, +0.5 counted), with Opp factor, Exp min, floor/ceiling, Owned %, Turn, and bank freed when cheaper. Uses official free trades/bank captions when Fan ID is configured. **Start best team** runs the picker; opening the tab does not. After My team is saved, Best team hides the last suggestion until Start is pressed again so Keep/New is not compared to an old lineup. Saved team on Best team follows the team last open on My team.

Coach points are the official margin buckets, not PIR: win 1–10 or OT +10, 11–20 +20, 21+ +25; loss 1–10 or OT −5, 11–20 −10, 21+ −20. Coach **Fpts/g**, **Last 5**, **Avg margin**, **Projected**, **Floor**, and **Ceiling** use that scale. The coach counts in full. Color coaches against other coaches. **Form** No games means the coach has no cached EuroLeague results.

Saved squads live in `data/squad.json` as named teams. The active name is the one open on My team. Optional **Import from Fantasy Challenge** on My team (button only) overwrites the active saved team with the official Fan ID lineup when the user confirms. Best team compares the suggestion to the **Saved team** you have selected: **Coming in** is new, **Going out** is dropped (including a coach change). Press **Start best team** after picking changes. **Copy this squad** writes the result into a named team.
